            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0364" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/577.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-17T13:00:00-04:49"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1911—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Furniss reports that Government officers admit that a strong undercurrent is
                    developing against the administration and he doubts the ability of the
                    Government to control the situation in case of an outbreak. The Government has
                    chartered a German vessel, which will arrive at Fort Liberté to take the
                    President on board to-morrow; its destination is unknown, but is presumed to be
                    Cape Haitien or Port au Prince.</p>
            </div>
